:''Not to be confused with [[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Tank Cat]]. For the weaker boss, see [[Wicked Tank Cat (Enemy)|Wicked Tank Cat]].
'''Malevolent Eraser Cat''' is an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemy that appears in [[Demon Eraser (Merciless)|The Malevolent Tank]]. It was added in [[Version 12.7 Update|Version 12.7]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Malevolent Eraser Cat
|image = E 661.png
|first appearance = [[Demon Eraser (Merciless)|The Malevolent Tank]]
|money drop = 2,000¢ - 7,900¢
}}

==Enemy==
This enemy is much more threatening than [[Manic Eraser Cat (Enemy)|Manic Eraser Cat]]. Though it has slightly less range, attacks slower, lacks Base Destroyer and has considerably lower damage, its strong Area Attacks still pack a huge punch. Each of its attacks generates a level 2 [[Surge Attack]]s that dramatically increases its reach, and it replicates any Surges your [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|cats]] may be using against it. Combined with the devastating peons in its stage, it can be more than a nightmare to handle despite retaining the same speed as Manic Eraser.

==Strategy==
This enemy's high range, significant damage and powerful surges all serve to quickly whittle down whatever units in play so supporting enemies can easily break through any defense. With its massive health as well, it's better to prepare an endurance battle with the use of surge-immune units, preferably those able to outrange it.

As with its traitless equivalents, this enemy isn't immune to status effects, so they can be used to greatly impede its advance.

